# What never enters the web build context.
#
# The root .dockerignore excludes `web/` from the api and worker builds; this file is its
# counterpart, and it is read because compose sets `context: ./web` (docker reads
# `<context>/.dockerignore`, not the one beside the compose file).
#
# Same two reasons as the root file, and they are worth keeping apart:
#
#   * SIZE - node_modules/ and .next/ together are the overwhelming majority of this directory.
#     Both are uploaded to the daemon on every build and both invalidate the cache constantly.
#     They are also actively harmful: node_modules/ was installed on the host, so any package
#     with a native binding would be the wrong platform inside a linux/amd64 image, and a stale
#     host .next/ can be picked up in place of the one the builder stage produces.
#   * SAFETY - `.env.local` and friends hold whatever the developer pointed this at. Excluded
#     here as well as in .gitignore, because the builder stage does `COPY . .` and a build arg
#     is visible in `docker history` while a baked-in layer is not even that visible.
#
# Anything the build needs must NOT be listed here: package.json, package-lock.json,
# next.config.mjs, tsconfig.json, tailwind/postcss config, app/, src/, the instrumentation
# hooks and next-env.d.ts are all required by `npm ci` and `next build`.

# ── Installed and generated trees ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Test-only: neither `npm ci` nor `next build` reads these ─────────────────────────────────────
# tsconfig.json's include is a bare **/*.ts glob, so dropping tests/ shrinks what tsc walks
# during the build's type check rather than breaking it - a glob that matches nothing is not an
# error. The suites run in CI on the host, never inside this image.
tests/
playwright.config.ts
vitest.config.ts
vitest.setup.ts
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# ── Version control, editors, CI ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.vercel/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# ── Docs: the image serves the site, it does not ship the prose about it ─────────────────────────
README.md

# ── Secrets: never in a build context ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.example is the committed template and carries no values, but there is no reason to copy
# it in either, and a narrower pattern would risk missing `.env.production.local`.
.env
.env.*
